# QX6: QAOA p=1 on the same tuning problem at 16..32 qubits (Aer statevector) vs exact, SA and random, and the picks
# on the real objective -> hsf2_work/runs/<stamp>_qx6_scaling/.  Needs a FINISHED QX2 loop (--source qx2: the
# surrogate is fitted on all its real evaluations); submit after tune_loop is done.
# Memory: the 32-qubit statevector is 34 GB in single precision and 69 GB in double precision (used only if Aer's
# single-precision check fails on the node); 48 GB covers every size up to 32 in single and up to 31 in double, and a
# size that does not fit is skipped and recorded, not crashed.  CERN batch gives 3 GB per requested core.
# Resume an evicted job: add --out <absolute path of the same qx6 folder> (finished sizes are kept).
# Self-contained: run.sh activates the Part-II venv and sets every HSF2_* path (getenv = False).
executable     = run.sh
arguments      = python -m hsf2 tune-scaling --source qx2 --model latest --split tune --threads 16 --max-memory-gb 46 --workers 4
getenv         = False
output         = logs/scaling_$(ClusterId).out
error          = logs/scaling_$(ClusterId).err
log            = logs/scaling_$(ClusterId).log
request_cpus   = 16
request_memory = 48000
+JobFlavour    = "tomorrow"
# e-mail to <user>@cern.ch when the job ends (success or failure)
notification   = Complete
queue
